Subject: [PATCH] make the subject LabelEncoder modality-aware

brain2qwerty_v1/main.py hardcodes event_types="Meg" in the subject
LabelEncoder. On the registered Pinet2024Eeg study the event type is
"Eeg", so the encoder matches zero events and Data.build() raises
ValueError: No events found for LabelEncoder before training starts.

This infers the modality from the extractor instead.

--- a/brain2qwerty_v1/main.py
+++ b/brain2qwerty_v1/main.py
@@ -68,7 +68,11 @@ class Data(pydantic.BaseModel):
         self.neuro.prepare(events)
         self.feature.prepare(events)
 
-        subject_id = ns.extractors.LabelEncoder(event_types="Meg", event_field="subject")
+        # the neuro extractor knows which modality it reads; don't assume MEG
+        modality = getattr(self.neuro, "event_types", None) or (
+            "Eeg" if type(self.neuro).__name__.startswith("Eeg") else "Meg"
+        )
+        subject_id = ns.extractors.LabelEncoder(event_types=modality, event_field="subject")
         subject_id.prepare(events)
         channel_positions = ChannelPositions2D(neuro=self.neuro)
         channel_positions.prepare(events)
